 ## Background
-Uniform NDC Point Sampling was introduced in the context of NeRF (Neural Radiance Fields) to address the issue of positional encoding sensitivity to scene scale and camera pose [S2]. The method transforms rays into an average camera frame and samples uniformly in NDC space, allowing the network to learn consistent features regardless of the original camera configuration [S2]. It was proposed as an alternative to logarithmic sampling, offering a linear sampling curve in NDC space that corresponds to a $1/x$ disparity distribution in original space [S2]. The approach is detailed in the original NeRF paper and subsequent works like DONeRF [S2].
+Uniform NDC Point Sampling was introduced in the context of NeRF (Neural Radiance Fields) to address positional encoding applied equally to foreground and background frequencies [S2]. The method transforms rays into an average camera frame and samples uniformly in NDC space, allowing the network to learn consistent features regardless of the original camera configuration [S2]. It was proposed as an alternative to logarithmic sampling, offering a linear sampling curve in NDC space that corresponds to a $1/x$ disparity distribution in original space [S2]. The approach is detailed in the original NeRF paper and subsequent works like DONeRF [S2].
 
